WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.380
Bill Duke, Actor/Filmmaker/Author: I’ll
give you another example, (it’s in my book)

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.889
in 1984 I was working very hard and when your
agent says “You’re tired.”

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:14.839
You’ve got to take a vacation.

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:18.550
My agent makes 10% of what you make.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.550
When your agent tells you to take a vacation,
you know you’re exhausted.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:27.831
So I took a vacation and went to Hawaii because
he had just gotten married and told me to

00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:30.000
stay at the hotel there by myself.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.340
I just wanted to totally chill.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.770
I was there for a week, I was there fore two
weeks I said “I want to come back to this

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.770
place.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.770
I’ve never been here.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:39.770
It’s beautiful.”

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:44.380
So I got in the plane called the Island Hoppers,
it goes from one island to another and they

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.380
do a ground tour and then go to another island.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:52.040
We were on our way to Maui from the Big Island
and it was a twin-engine plane.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.125
And then all the sudden the plane started
going [makes sputtering noises].

00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:55.960
So we all stopped and said “What the heck?”

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:01.590
And it stopped so we started laughing you
know?

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:11.080
As soon as we laughed it went [more sputtering
noises] and the fellow said “Sit down!

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.080
Sit down!

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.080
Sit down!

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.080
Sit down!

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.500
Sit down and buckle your seats.”

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:28.880
Now usually in the movies when a plane is
in trouble the pilot says “Ladies and Gentlemen,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.780
be calm, be still, we’re in control.”

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:38.799
Little bit about the pilot…the pilot was
doing “Help us Jesus.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:39.799
Help us Mary.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:40.799
Help us Lord.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:41.799
Help us Jesus.

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:42.799
Help us Mary.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:43.810
Help us Lord.”

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:44.850
The pilot!

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.420
I look out the window and say “Damn, we
sure are close to the…BAMMMM!”

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.820
We crashed in the water.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.200
Now water seems soft, right?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.350
When you hit the water from that height it
went BAM, BAM.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.620
It tore the bolts out of my seat and threw
me forward.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:05.290
This scar is from that happening.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:14.330
And when that happened…it’s hard to explain
but it’s an out-of-body experience…something

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:22.270
up there looked down and I know it sounds
crazy but down at me and my seat, all the

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:26.190
people hurt, the pilot and everything.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:32.610
So this thing I can’t explain what it was,
it’s peaceful, just observing…me.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:38.110
The pilot wakes up.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:43.880
His face hit the dashboard of the plane “Everybody
up!

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.069
Get out!”

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:51.629
This thing and my body merged back together
and they said out loud (because I don’t

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:53.870
swim) I said “Bill…”

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:59.070
I said it out loud “You’re always wanted
to know how you’re going to die, now you

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.800
know.”

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:01.890
I just sat there waiting.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.940
The water is coming up…boom, boom, boom.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.890
Is coming up…boom, boom, boom.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:10.450
Pilot gets these people out, takes them to
the wing he says “Hey you!

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.550
C’mon, let’s go, let’s go, let’s go!”

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.349
I said “I can’t swim.”

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:19.010
He says “[Sighs] Unbuckle your seat.”

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.530
Okay I unbuckle my seat.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.410
“Take the life donut out.”

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.520
I’ve thrown it up.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.200
“Put it around your head.”

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.120
He gives me instructions.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.269
“Pull the chords.”

00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:32.450
When I read the brochure there were about
five chords.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:36.200
I looked down and saw a thousand and kept
pulling them and pulling them and pulling

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.640
them and nothing happened.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.610
He said “Come to the wing!”

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.610
I said “I don’t see.”

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.099
He said “Come to the wing!”

00:03:43.099 --> 00:03:46.370
I got to the wing.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:51.460
I’m standing there and they all paddled
away because they all see family and everything,

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.250
they are 500-600 feet away and he says “Jump!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.250
Jump!

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.250
Undertow!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.250
Undertow!”

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.250
I said “I can’t swim.”

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.250
He says “Jump!”

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.040
I say to myself “What the hell do I have
to lose.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.470
I’m going to die anyway.”

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:11.459
So I jumped and I forgot to tie the life donut
around my waist because he had pulled the

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:13.629
chord as I passed him.

00:04:13.629 --> 00:04:14.840
It blew up.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.629
I’ve got it tied around my waist.

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:25.469
I went down once, twice, third time I came
up…life donut (I’m not exaggerating) the

00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:28.710
life donut is here [by his head].

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:36.589
I put it around my head like a little dog,
I do like this [paddles] and I reach them.

00:04:36.589 --> 00:04:45.960
I recently turned around, this big mouth of
water swallows the plane and takes it under,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.849
if I stayed on the wing I would have died.

00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:56.719
I’m telling this all the truth.

00:04:56.719 --> 00:04:59.009
In the water, ten minutes passes.

00:04:59.009 --> 00:05:00.710
People are moaning and groaning.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.199
A lady says “Look!

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:04.250
Boats, planes, boats, planes.”

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:10.020
I my thought is before you die because there’s
sharks in the world and everything you have

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.080
these delusional thoughts and you think you
see things.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.149
That’s what she’s doing, right?

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:20.839
So I says [makes dismissive sound].

00:05:20.839 --> 00:05:23.309
“Boats, planes, boats, planes.”

00:05:23.309 --> 00:05:29.089
Take this to Vegas, you tell me the chances
of this happening.

00:05:29.089 --> 00:05:41.009
Twice a year the Hawaii Fire Department sends
its emergency rescue teams out to do practices

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:49.789
in all different parts of the ocean.

00:05:49.789 --> 00:06:00.389
This day they were one half nautical miles
away from us.

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:02.569
They saw the plane go in.

00:06:02.569 --> 00:06:11.050
They were there in minutes.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:22.819
They took everybody out of the water, wrapped
us in blankets, asked if we were okay and

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:27.089
started driving us back to shore.

00:06:27.089 --> 00:06:34.439
I sat next to the pilot, six foot three Ichabod
Crane, blue eyes.

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:36.889
I could see his face, dark hair with white
streaks.

00:06:36.889 --> 00:06:39.410
He’s shivering, I’m shivering, he’s
sitting.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:48.159
And I say to him “Sir I don’t want to
disturb you but I was in shock.

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:50.009
You talked me through getting out of the plane.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:55.649
You talked me into jumping off the wing, you
talked me to paddling toward…you saved my

00:06:55.649 --> 00:06:57.750
life and I want to thank you.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.139
I cannot know what to say?”

00:07:02.139 --> 00:07:06.159
He looks at me and he says “I appreciate
you saying this.”

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:09.240
He says “I’m a Catholic.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.559
I believe in Jesus Christ.”

00:07:12.559 --> 00:07:15.729
He says “I don’t know what you believe
in?”

00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:18.949
He says “…But don’t thank me.

00:07:18.949 --> 00:07:22.150
Thank that.”

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:30.059
Turns away from me, looks back in my face,
grabs my shoulder, and starts crying like

00:07:30.059 --> 00:07:31.759
a baby.

00:07:31.759 --> 00:07:53.419
I get back to shore and people are in shock
because planes that crash in that part of

00:07:53.419 --> 00:08:01.430
the water don’t have survivors.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:09.620
I have no way of explaining it to say that
that is one of the days I realized that there

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:17.139
are things happening in this Universe that
are far beyond my intellect…far beyond my

00:08:17.139 --> 00:08:20.629
intellect.

00:08:20.629 --> 00:08:33.979
And I had my two Master’s degrees and I
was so smart…[scoffs]…I can’t even tell

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:37.719
you how much I learned from that experience.

00:08:37.719 --> 00:08:43.169
I have pictures on the wall in my condo up
there of that day from the newspaper.

00:08:43.169 --> 00:08:46.170
I saved it and just framed it.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.580
I never want to forget it.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.759
So it shaped my life.

00:08:52.759 --> 00:09:00.550
Between those experiences and meditation,
it shaped my life and made me understand that…you

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:01.930
know…

